phase-038 critical Implement `might fail`, the documented non-aborting form of a fallible call
phase-039 major Test or delete the 21 public assertion functions nothing calls
phase-040 major Parse `repeat ... until` as the post-test loop SPEC.md documents
phase-041 major Implement `text.split` and `text.join`, and pin which stdlib names are reachable dotted
phase-042 minor VS Code extension: snippets, run command and keybindings
phase-043 minor WebAssembly playground: compile the interpreter to WASM
phase-044 major Package manager: manifest, versions and lockfile
phase-045 major Debugger: breakpoints, stepping and frame inspection in the REPL
phase-046 minor Rich errors: suggestions and rendered diagnostics
phase-047 blocker Substitute `{expr}` in string literals so `Expr::InterpolatedText` is reachable
phase-048 critical Make `catch error <name>` bind the message, as SPEC.md and README.md spell it
phase-049 major Stop reserving nine keywords the parser cannot read, or document them
phase-050 major Reconcile SPEC.md's stdlib module names with src/stdlib.rs MODULES
phase-051 blocker Delete the uncommitted S3 work sitting in a checkout whose phase is marked .done
phase-052 critical Wire the REPL to a real line editor: TAB completion, persistent history, sane interrupts
phase-053 major Give the REPL a color system: TTY detection, forced modes, and one theme
phase-054 major Highlight Redblue code live as it is typed, using Redblue's own lexer
phase-055 major Polish the session surface: banner, prompt, numbered continuations, and `!!`
phase-056 major Teach the REPL to answer questions about code: `.type`, `.doc`, `.which`, `.sighelp`
phase-057 major Let the REPL measure code: `.time` and `.bench`
phase-058 major Show the compiler inside the REPL: `.bytecode` and `.asm`
phase-059 major Make REPL errors point at the code: source context through the color system
phase-060 major Export sessions and complete file paths: `.export` plus TAB for `:load`/`:save`
phase-061 major Complete after the dot, edit in `$EDITOR`, and teach newcomers: member completion, `.edit`, `:tutorial`
phase-062 major Open a debug sub-REPL: `.debug` with `.watch`, `.stack` and `.locals`
phase-063 major Print values three ways: `.pretty`, `.json`, `.table`
phase-064 major Close the file loop: `.reload`, `.format`, and format-on-enter
phase-065 major Let users extend the REPL: `.alias` and `.macro`
phase-066 major Settle engine arguments with evidence: `.compare` runs both engines
phase-067 major Give the session a memory: `.checkpoint`, `.restore`, `.undo`, `.redo`, `.sessions`
phase-068 major Talk to the shell without leaving: `!cmd`, `.pipe`, `.cd`, `.pwd`, `.ls`
phase-069 major Find things without leaving: `.search` across docs, history, bindings and help
phase-070 major Weigh the session: `.mem` and `.profile`
phase-071 major Map the whole environment: `.env`, `.types`, `.dir`, `.typehints`
phase-072 major Let the session switch engines: `.vm` toggles tree-walker and bytecode VM
phase-073 major Measure before optimizing: a benchmark harness with a checked-in baseline
phase-074 major Hash the self-hosted compiler's intern table instead of scanning it
phase-075 major Teach the language server navigation: goto-definition, references, completion
phase-076 major Scaffold projects: `rb new`, root discovery, and a project-aware `rb test`
phase-077 major Finish the list surface: `sort`, `reverse`, `zip`, `enumerate`, `filter`, `reduce`
